### Breaking

- Require Node.js 22. (#1243)  04b4454

- The subprocess is now a normal promise, instead of a [`ChildProcess`](https://nodejs.org/api/child_process.html#class-childprocess) instance augmented with promise methods. All the methods and properties [documented by Execa](docs/api.md#subprocess) are unchanged. Node.js-specific `ChildProcess` APIs (such as `.on()`, `.send()`, `.ref()` and `.unref()`) must now be accessed through the new [`subprocess.nodeChildProcess`](docs/api.md#subprocessnodechildprocess) property. (#1255)  ade74bf

```diff
const subprocess = execa('node', ['file.js']);
- subprocess.on('spawn', onSpawn);
+ subprocess.nodeChildProcess.on('spawn', onSpawn);
```

- Removed `execaCommand()` and `execaCommandSync()`. Use the [template string syntax](docs/execution.md#template-string-syntax) instead, which splits on spaces. If the command is a dynamic string, split it with [`parseCommandString()`](docs/api.md#parsecommandstringcommand). (#1244)  3ced394

```diff
- await execaCommand('npm run build');
+ await execa`npm run build`;

- await execaCommand(commandString);
+ await execa`${parseCommandString(commandString)}`;
```

- Removed the old undocumented `stdio: [..., 'ipc']` syntax. Use the [`ipc: true`](docs/api.md#optionsipc) option instead. (#1245)  dcf611c

```diff
- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe', 'ipc']});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {ipc: true});
```

- When the [`input`](docs/api.md#optionsinput) or [`inputFile`](docs/api.md#optionsinputfile) option is combined with an inherited [`stdin`](docs/api.md#optionsstdin) (for example `stdio: 'inherit'`), the explicit input is now used, instead of being ignored. To combine [multiple inputs](docs/input.md#multiple-inputs), pass an array like `stdin: ['inherit', {string: 'input'}]`. (#1232)  3ed0544

### Improvements

- Terminate the subprocess' [descendant processes](docs/termination.md#killing-descendant-processes) by using the [`killDescendants`](docs/api.md#optionskilldescendants) option. This is useful when the subprocess spawns its own processes, such as when using the [`shell`](docs/api.md#optionsshell) option. (#1256)  84fa0ec

```js
await execa('npm', ['run', 'build'], {killDescendants: true, timeout: 5000});
```

- [Convert the subprocess](docs/streams.md#converting-a-subprocess-to-a-web-stream) to a web stream by using [`subprocess.readableStream()`](docs/api.md#subprocessreadablestreamreadableoptions), [`subprocess.writableStream()`](docs/api.md#subprocesswritablestreamwritableoptions) or [`subprocess.transformStream()`](docs/api.md#subprocesstransformstreamduplexoptions). (#1254)  29d9cfc

```js
await execa`npm run build`
	.readableStream()
	.pipeTo(writableWebStream);
```

- The value returned by [`subprocess.pipe()`](docs/api.md#subprocesspipefile-arguments-options) now exposes the destination subprocess' methods, so the piped output can be consumed directly: [iterate](docs/pipe.md#iterate-stream-and-ipc) over its output lines, [convert it to a stream](docs/streams.md#converting-a-subprocess-to-a-stream), or [exchange IPC messages](docs/ipc.md#exchanging-messages). (#1252)  c31c94c

```js
for await (const line of execa`npm run build`.pipe`sort`) {
	console.log(line);
}
```

- Use an [additional file descriptor as input](docs/input.md#additional-file-descriptors) by wrapping its [`stdio`](docs/api.md#optionsstdio) value as a `{value, input: true}` object. Direction-ambiguous values (`'pipe'`, `'inherit'`, [files](docs/input.md#file-input) and [transforms](docs/transform.md)) default to output on additional file descriptors. (#1246, #1249)  487a3a4 9fbf5ba

```js
const subprocess = execa({stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe', {value: 'pipe', input: true}]})`npm run scaffold`;

const writable = subprocess.writable({to: 'fd3'});
```

- The [transform](docs/transform.md) generator function's `chunk` argument is now typed based on the transform's mode, instead of always being `unknown`: `string` for line transforms, `Uint8Array` for [binary transforms](docs/binary.md#transforms), and `unknown` in [object mode](docs/transform.md#object-mode). (#1247)  0a7b4f8

### Fixes

- Fixed [fd-specific options](docs/output.md#stdoutstderr-specific-options) ([`verbose`](docs/api.md#optionsverbose), [`maxBuffer`](docs/api.md#optionsmaxbuffer), etc.) when the [`ipc`](docs/api.md#optionsipc) option is `true`: `fd3` and `ipc` no longer target the same file descriptor. (#1241)  b886883

